": "Delaware enters the 2028 presidential race as a structurally Democratic state, with a partisan lean of eight points toward the Democrats and a long record of supporting the party's presidential nominees. The seat is open, with a term-limited incumbent Republican president leaving the ballot without either party's incumbent, and no candidate fundraising or outside spending has been reported.\n\nNo public polls of Delaware's general election are available and no expert ratings have been published, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan balance. That points to an expected Democratic margin of about eight points, with wide uncertainty given the absence of direct polling. The race is rated Lean D: the Democrat starts with a clear structural edge, but the 2028 national environment and the yet-unknown nominees on both sides leave room for movement in either direction.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8204, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7838, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7798, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7761, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7732, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8108, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7706, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7752, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7784, "margin": 8.0}]}